<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech govt approves new CZK 1.05 bln flood funds.</title>
<headline>Czech govt approves new CZK 1.05 bln flood funds.</headline>
<dateline>KOLODEJE, Czech Republic 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech government approved an additional 1.05 billion crowns in funds from the state budget for flood relief programmes in the eastern part of the country, Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference during a cabinet meeting at a chateau east of Prague, Klaus said another 250 million crowns would be used for flood relief from the off-budget state agricultural land fund.</p>
</text>
